.SH "NAME"
pcre2_get_subject \- get a match subject pointer
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBPCRE2_SPTR\fP pcre2_get_subject(\fBpcre2_match_data\fP *\fImatch_data\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
After a successful match, a partial match, or a failure to match, this function
returns the subject pointer that was passed to the matching function. For a
successful match with \fBPCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT\fP, it returns a pointer to
a copy of the subject that is owned by the match data block instead. The copy
contains exactly the subject length that was passed to the matching function and
is not necessarily zero\-terminated. It is freed when the match data block is
reused for another match or is freed. The returned pointer must not be used after
that.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.